A learner in Masvingo writes this text-based game. The player walks along a path of cells 0 to 5; cell 3 has a thorn bush and cell 4 has a prize. The player types R to move right and L to move left. The five commands typed are R, R, R, R, R.

```python
position = 0
lives = 2
score = 0
hazards = {3}
prizes = {4}
turns = 0
while lives > 0 and position < 5:
    move = input()
    turns = turns + 1
    if move == "R":
        position = position + 1
    elif move == "L" and position > 0:
        position = position - 1
    if position in hazards:
        lives = lives - 1
        print("Hit a thorn bush")
    if position in prizes:
        score = score + 5
        print("Found a prize")
print("Lives", lives, "score", score, "turns", turns)
```
